Makes the version table in sim.rs `record` replace a record under a vector it
already holds only when kind, hash, exec bit or deletion state differ, as
before 8d4620d. A re-issue after a revert with the same content but a later
mtime then keeps the discarded record, and I4 checks the node's conflict-copy
names against an mtime nobody holds any more (DESIGN.md §14.1 I4 and I7,
§8.3).

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_reissued_vector_replaces_the_discarded_record_whatever_its_content
test: delocal-sim sim::tests::a_reissued_vector_replaces_the_discarded_record_with_the_same_content

